# The power service (power(8), D130): every CPU with ACPI's CPPC at its
# highest performance level, its desired-performance registers written
# through the SCMI agent's ctl (D167: the agent owns their page, power
# maps no memory); the thermal zones read at their period,
# a step down at a passive trip and power-off at a critical one, through
# devmgr's /dev/reboot. devmgr's `cpus` and `thermal` say what there is.
service power
program power
export
use devmgr
mount /dev devmgr/dev
restart on-failure
